# antAI — Hackathon Pitch Deck Content
# Track: Real-Time Scam and Impersonation Defense (Problem ID-IHNG6)
#
# Every claim below is tagged so Q&A knows instantly what to defend:
#   [BUILT & WORKING]              — implemented and exercised
#   [BUILT BUT NOT VERIFIED/TESTED]— implemented, not yet validated on hardware
#   [DESIGNED, NOT YET BUILT]      — planned/scaffolded, not live
#   [NEEDS EXTERNAL RESEARCH]      — needs a citation added by you
#
# Framed favorably but factually. Nothing below is fabricated.

================================================================================
1. PROBLEM STATEMENT
================================================================================

- The brief (Problem ID-IHNG6) "Real-Time Scam and Impersonation Defense":
  scams now combine social engineering with AI-generated text, realistic
  impersonation, and voice cloning, so keyword/link/sender filters fail because
  the attack LOOKS like an ordinary conversation. [BUILT & WORKING]

- The attack has shifted from "obvious spam" to "credible conversation" -
  urgency, impersonation, and emotional pressure instead of links and
  known-bad senders. [BUILT & WORKING — we coded against exactly this: urgency
  scorer, intent classifier, and identity/voice signals target these, not
  keyword matching]

- A warning is not enough — the brief demands a PROTECTIVE ACTION (freeze a
  request, notify a trusted contact, log an incident) before harm is done.
  [BUILT & WORKING — Freeze/Intercept + Verify-with-trusted-contact + post-call
  report are all implemented]

- The verdict must never be a black box — it must EXPLAIN its reasoning in
  plain language. [BUILT & WORKING — the LLM reasoner outputs verdict / why /
  action in plain language]

- Target users: elderly and vulnerable users who are most susceptible to
  pressure/impersonation scams. [BUILT & WORKING — the LLM system prompt
  explicitly addresses "elderly and vulnerable users"; the UI uses large,
  plain-language verdict cards and blunt two-button confirm dialogs, not
  technical scores]

- Market size / prevalence statistics: none exist in the repo.
  [NEEDS EXTERNAL RESEARCH — add a cited scam-loss figure here yourself]

================================================================================
2. SOLUTION APPROACH
================================================================================

- One-liner: antAI is a real-time scam-and-impersonation defense layer that
  scores live calls, messages, and notifications across multiple signals,
  explains its reasoning in plain language, and ACTS (freeze / verify / warn)
  when risk is high. [BUILT & WORKING]

- Multi-signal fusion, not keyword matching — risk is a weighted fusion of 9+
  independent signals: scam-pattern text, urgency/pressure, actionable request
  intent, behavioral deviation, voice authenticity (synthetic-voice), video
  authenticity (deepfake), lip-sync mismatch, identity mismatch, and collective
  community flags. [BUILT & WORKING — fusion_node in orchestration/nodes.py]

- Dual channel — the protected user is covered on every surface: (1) in-app
  voice/video calls, and (2) SMS + third-party-app notifications from ANY sender
  on the public network (a scammer needs to install nothing for the SMS /
  notification channel). [BUILT & WORKING — SmsReceiver,
  AntaiNotificationListenerService, /api/notify/external]

- Explainable by design — every output is plain-language
  "verdict -> why -> what to do now", never a raw score. [BUILT & WORKING —
  reasoner.py generate_verdict / generate_live_guidance]

- Protective escalation ladder — passive log -> verify-with-trusted-contact ->
  freeze/intercept -> critical pause-with-disclaimer. [BUILT & WORKING —
  decision_node + intercept/ + trust_circle/]

- Agentic orchestration — a native LangGraph state machine routes each event
  (voice/video vs text) through only the relevant detectors. [BUILT & WORKING —
  orchestration/graph.py]

- In-app calling is the clean-audio channel for the protected user and their
  trusted circle. [BUILT & WORKING]

- Full real-cellular-call screening (default-dialer / CallScreeningService /
  InCallService) is the next phase. [DESIGNED, NOT YET BUILT —
  ANTAI_V3_DEVICE_LEVEL_PLAN.md sections 4-8]

================================================================================
3. WORKFLOW (actual end-to-end call chain)
================================================================================

Live call (app-to-app WebRTC + analysis tap):
- 1. Phone A <-> Phone B establish a WebRTC call via the Node.js signaling
  server (SimpleVideoCallBackend/server.js, port 3007). [BUILT & WORKING]
- 2. In parallel, each phone opens a SECOND, send-only WebRTC peer connection to
  the antAI server (/ws/tap, AiTapEngine.kt -> gateway/tap.py), carrying a copy
  of its mic/camera. The real call stays P2P and untouched. [BUILT & WORKING]
- 3. The server's aiortc SFU decodes the tapped media and forks every frame into
  ingestion (media_sfu/tap_session.py, media_sfu/tracks.py). [BUILT & WORKING]
- 4. Audio -> Silero VAD segments speech (ingestion/audio.py) -> Deepgram ASR
  (or local faster-whisper) -> live transcript. Video -> 6 fps frame sampler
  (ingestion/frames.py). [BUILT & WORKING]
- 5. Each audio segment / 24-frame batch triggers the LangGraph pipeline
  (SessionRunner in orchestration/dispatcher.py): router -> voice-deepfake +
  video-deepfake -> identity -> collective-DB -> urgency -> intent -> fusion ->
  decision -> LLM. [BUILT & WORKING]
- 6. Verdict / guidance / transcript / per-model signals are pushed over
  WebSocket (RealtimeHub) to both phones and rendered in the in-call "antAI"
  overlay window (AiInsightWindow.kt). [BUILT & WORKING]

Message / notification:
- 7. Chat message (/ws/chat or /api/chat/send) or SMS / notification
  (/api/notify/external) -> keyword triage gate -> same text/urgency/intent/
  fusion/LLM path -> verdict pushed; high-risk messages intercepted before
  delivery. [BUILT & WORKING]

Protective actions (live):
- 8. risk >= 70 + actionable request -> Freeze/Intercept (holds OTP/money/
  credential/link action with an override). [BUILT & WORKING —
  intercept/controller.py]
- 9. Synthetic voice / deepfake video / credential ask / identity mismatch ->
  call pauses with a "Possible scam" disclaimer popup on both phones.
  [BUILT & WORKING]
- 10. "Verify who this really is" -> REST /api/verify/request -> trusted contact
  gets a Yes/No prompt -> result drives the in-call bar + verdict.
  [BUILT & WORKING]

================================================================================
4. KEY FEATURES & INNOVATION
================================================================================

Live & working:
- Real-time scam scoring on live calls (voice + video) with a continuous risk
  band (monitoring / caution / high-risk). [BUILT & WORKING]
- Synthetic-voice detection — SSL ensemble (AST-ASVspoof5 + wav2vec2 deepfake-
  voice detector) with a Modulate Velma-2 hosted fallback. [BUILT & WORKING —
  exact models read from deepfake_voice.py / providers.py]
- Video deepfake detection — ensemble of CommunityForensics DeepfakeDet-ViT
  (CVPR 2025) + DiCoME (evidential CLIP + LoRA head). [BUILT & WORKING]
- Scam-pattern text classifier — fine-tuned DistilBERT over 8 scam types
  (family-emergency, OTP, bank, prize, job, romance, remote-access, gift-card),
  bilingual EN/Hindi. [BUILT & WORKING]
- Urgency/pressure scorer + request/intent classifier (money / OTP / credential
  / remote-access / link). [BUILT & WORKING]
- Behavioral-deviation model (sentence-transformers) — flags "Dad suddenly
  writing in a different register asking for money". [BUILT & WORKING]
- Plain-language LLM reasoning — self-hosted Qwen2.5-3B (llama.cpp) with a Groq
  hosted fallback; emits verdict/why/action + post-call report. [BUILT & WORKING]
- Freeze/Intercept — holds OTP/money/credential/link actions mid-conversation
  with a conscious override (never a silent block). [BUILT & WORKING]
- Verify-with-trusted-contact — the "is this really you?" escalation to a linked
  family member. [BUILT & WORKING]
- Collective flagging DB — hash-based, reputation-weighted community scam flags.
  [BUILT & WORKING]
- SMS + notification guard — reads incoming SMS and other-app notifications,
  scans them, no sender cooperation needed. [BUILT & WORKING]
- Live transcript streaming and per-model signal streaming into the UI.
  [BUILT & WORKING]

Security / privacy (actual code, not aspiration):
- Phone numbers encrypted at rest (Fernet, storage/crypto.py). [BUILT & WORKING]
- Collective flags stored as SHA-256 hashes, never raw PII. [BUILT & WORKING]
- Voiceprints stored as embeddings only (raw audio not retained).
  [BUILT & WORKING]
- API keys in gitignored .env, never committed. [BUILT & WORKING]

Scaffolded / designed, not yet active (say "on the roadmap", not "live"):
- Voiceprint identity match (ECAPA-TDNN) — enrolment endpoint exists, matching
  model currently disabled. [DESIGNED, NOT YET BUILT — speaker_verify
  enabled:false in config.yaml]
- DeCoF fully-AI-video detector — wired, weights not released.
  [DESIGNED, NOT YET BUILT]
- Real cellular-call screening (ROLE_CALL_SCREENING / ROLE_DIALER).
  [DESIGNED, NOT YET BUILT]

