================================================================================
6. FEASIBILITY & VIABILITY
================================================================================

- It runs end-to-end today — server boots, all detection engines load, and the
  full call -> pipeline -> verdict -> UI loop has been exercised on two real
  phones. [BUILT & WORKING]

- Graceful degradation built in — every model is lazy-loaded with a fail-soft
  fallback; a missing model/API degrades to a heuristic and the pipeline never
  crashes the call. [BUILT & WORKING — hub.py + per-engine fallbacks]

- Real cost drivers (actual paid APIs called): Deepgram, Modulate Velma, Groq —
  per-call/per-token. [BUILT & WORKING]

- Cost-offramp already coded: each of the three hosted APIs can be switched back
  to a LOCAL model (faster-whisper, local SSL voice ensemble, local Qwen GGUF)
  by flipping one config value — so a live demo can run fully offline at zero
  API cost. [BUILT & WORKING — providers.* backend selectors in config.yaml]

- Latency-conscious design — heavy model calls run off the event loop
  (asyncio.to_thread), the media relay is never stalled, and the transcript/LLM
  stream in the background. [BUILT & WORKING]

- Known constraint (frame positively): call analysis requires the app on both
  ends (app-to-app); the SMS/notification channel already works for any external
  sender, and real-call screening is the stated next phase.
  [BUILT & WORKING + DESIGNED]

